{
  "area": "quests-lifecycle-rows",
  "description": "Hand cases for the quest lifecycle rows (PL.native-quest-lifecycle-rows): what core's corpus conformance/quests/lifecycle.json leaves unpinned — the contract row whole against core's exports, a batch of several steps in one apply (one result per op, in order, a refused step inside it changing nothing), the facts and quests rows, the default player and an empty batch, core's own refusals as values through the rows, the [invalid-input] boundary of the members core reads unchecked (only where core does not refuse the same set itself), and the session's kind, handle and ops checks. Every expectation is computed by core's own lifecycle at the pin (gen-bridge-lifecycle-cases.mts, kept with the builder's record); each boundary expectation is asserted to be a set core does not refuse as a value.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "quest.lifecycle.contract states core's exported tables: the statuses, the step ops, the host-event dispatch, the refusal codes, the default player, the fact predicates and the completion criteria types",
      "steps": [
        {
          "call": "quest.lifecycle.contract",
          "args": {},
          "expect": {
            "statuses": [
              "unavailable",
              "available",
              "active",
              "completed"
            ],
            "ops": [
              "offer",
              "accept",
              "talk_to",
              "reach",
              "pick_up",
              "deliver",
              "read",
              "find_clue",
              "find_text",
              "read_sign",
              "use_word",
              "pronounce",
              "identify",
              "answer_listening",
              "use_grammar"
            ],
            "hostEventDispatch": {
              "talk_to": [
                "npc_talked",
                "npc_conversation"
              ],
              "reach": [
                "location_visited",
                "location_discovered"
              ],
              "pick_up": [
                "item_collected"
              ],
              "deliver": [
                "item_delivered"
              ],
              "read": [
                "text_read"
              ],
              "find_clue": [
                "clue_discovered"
              ],
              "find_text": [
                "text_found"
              ],
              "read_sign": [
                "sign_read"
              ],
              "use_word": [
                "vocabulary_usage"
              ],
              "pronounce": [
                "pronunciation_attempt"
              ],
              "identify": [
                "object_identified"
              ],
              "answer_listening": [
                "listening_graded"
              ],
              "use_grammar": [
                "grammar_demonstrated"
              ]
            },
            "refusalCodes": [
              "missing_field",
              "duplicate_quest",
              "duplicate_objective",
              "bad_status",
              "unknown_op",
              "unknown_quest",
              "not_available",
              "prerequisites_unmet",
              "not_giver",
              "bad_count",
              "bad_criteria",
              "bad_score",
              "bad_time"
            ],
            "defaultPlayer": "player",
            "predicates": [
              "quest_status",
              "quest_offered",
              "objective_complete",
              "objective_progress",
              "quest_progress",
              "experience_granted",
              "item_granted"
            ],
            "criteriaTypes": [
              "all_objectives",
              "conversation_turns"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "one session through every row: a batch of five ops answers one result each in order (an offer, the accept that clears it, a pick-up stack of two, a step core refuses as a value, which changes nothing, and a talk the lock holds), a second batch completes the quest at its atMs and activates the follow-up; the facts and quests rows read the session; a disposed session is gone",
      "steps": [
        {
          "call": "quest.lifecycle.create",
          "args": {
            "player": "hero",
            "quests": [
              {
                "id": "q_herbs",
